86482544 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}x & =5-{x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-10 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(2x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard the solution $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ since $x\\le 0$ in our region. Therefore, $x$-limits are $-2\\le x\\le 0.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/5b/5bafe1d8cd35eec83aba3a9a24f777340a09f824919d4cedc5879c774e30cf5e.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}x\\le y\\le 5-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x/2}^{5-{x}^{2}}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482622 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "09dc735b-be54-5f55-a40c-b3de9cb3c25f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482622 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482646 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186482657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482646 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1d9c3ed-33de-5684-8d99-d7f5f9b0c7e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482646 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482654 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186482656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482654 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e0bceb01-13f0-500a-a70e-d7c56dc36189" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482654 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482656 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186482646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482656 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ed3c1020-e19e-5ebc-82db-39b373afe65a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482656 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759